# Domain cutover reminder (Cloudflare / DNS)

When the user asks to set up **Cloudflare**, **DNS**, or cut over **`maddysfoundation.org`** for this project:

1. Point DNS (Cloudflare preferred) at the Vercel project `maddys-foundation`.
2. Add `maddysfoundation.org` (+ `www`) in Vercel → Domains.
3. **Required:** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://maddysfoundation.org` on Vercel (Production + Preview) — replace the temporary `https://maddys-foundation.vercel.app` value.
4. Redeploy production (`vercel --prod` or push) so `metadataBase`, Open Graph, and absolute URLs use the real domain (OG images 404’d on the parked domain before).
5. Also update `lib/site-metadata.ts` if it still special-cases / ignores `maddysfoundation.org` for OG — remove that guard once DNS resolves correctly.
6. Smoke-check: `/opengraph-image.jpg` and home `og:image` resolve on `https://maddysfoundation.org`.

Do this as part of the Cloudflare/DNS task — don’t stop at DNS-only.
